Cell["What this notebook is for", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"80749fb5-20d5-4446-b067-5e2b1cb59fe8"],

Cell["\<\
Computed or visualized here means: Wolfram evaluates exact limits, matrix \
formulas, determinants, congruence calculations, and visual summaries of \
formulas already present in the paper and Lean files.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"93bc959b-2da4-4153-b0fb-ac77c5976d6c"],

Cell["\<\
Formally proved in Lean means: theorem names and proof-structure claims come \
from local Lean modules, not from Wolfram. Interpretive framing comes from \
the paper.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c0ee0faf-8e5c-423d-89bc-06ef12cf74ef"],

Cell["One parameter, three worlds", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4552e272-3f3e-4fa3-b932-fab58226846d"],

Cell["\<\
The paper's starting point is a single kappa-controlled family of \
inertial-frame transformations. The sign of kappa is not interpreted first; \
the notebook computes the shared structure and then reads the branch split \
from the invariant form.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f66bbed7-dd2f-46fe-aeb6-48058b7289d3"],

